          "message": "feat: implement Docker volume attach/detach via container recreation\n\nDocker does not support hot-attaching bind mounts to running containers,\nso we use a stop→recreate→start cycle. This enables persistent volume\nsupport for Docker-based compute instances.\n\nChanges:\n- Update ComputeBackend.AttachVolume/DetachVolume to return new container ID\n- Implement DockerAdapter volume attach/detach using stop→recreate→start\n- Add per-container locking via sync.Map to prevent concurrent operations\n- Update VolumeService to call compute backend and track ContainerID changes\n- Add comprehensive tests for the new functionality\n- Update docs (FEATURES, architecture, database, libvirt-backend, snapshots)\n- Add ADR-024 documenting the decision\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: AttachVolume/DetachVolume signatures changed to return\nnew container ID for proper instance tracking.\n\nTests: Docker adapter (35 passing), Libvirt adapter (30 passing),\nVolumeService with ComputeBackend (4 new tests passing)",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-14T19:31:47+03:00",
          "tree_id": "29fb9e1cd2c2e87f019ae377398157bfef960d7e",
          "url": "https://github.com/poyrazK/thecloud/commit/a1caa0919bbaaaae92db0a86111668c0991cd3ef"
