          "distinct": true,
          "id": "72bbd780b747285b7b56eb2578cd0f211e2e4a1a",
          "message": "feat: add configurable CPU for serverless functions (#549)\n\n* feat: add configurable CPU for serverless functions\n\n- Add CPUs float64 field to Function struct with range 0.1-8.0 cores\n- Add CPUs *float64 to FunctionUpdate with validation\n- Update SetColumns() for dynamic SQL updates\n- Add database migration 110_add_function_cpus\n- Update repository Create/Update/scanFunction for cpus column\n- Set default CPUs: 0.5 in CreateFunction\n- Use f.CPUs instead of hardcoded 0.5 in buildTaskOptions\n- Wire CPUs field through to UpdateFunctionRequest handler\n\n* test: add CPU validation tests for function updates\n\n- Add cpu_too_low and cpu_too_high test cases\n- Update valid test to include CPU: valid_timeout_memory_cpu\n\n* fix: update function repository tests to include cpus field\n\nThe function repository tests were missing the cpus column in their\nmock expectations and row definitions. This caused test failures\nbecause the actual repository queries now include the cpus column.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Poyraz <poyraz@example.com>",
